Phase 10.2 — Core auth infrastructure
------------------------------------------------------------------------

CREATE next-app/lib/server/provision.ts — workspace auto-provisioning:
  provisionWorkspace(userId, displayName):
    - Check if user already has a WorkspaceMember (idempotent)
    - If not, create Workspace + WorkspaceMember in a $transaction
    - Workspace name: "{displayName}'s Workspace"
    - WorkspaceMember role: "owner"
    - Called from Auth.js createUser event in auth.ts
    - Replaces ensureSingleUserSeed() from bootstrap.ts

CREATE next-app/lib/server/auth.ts — the key function:
  requireAuth(): Promise<ServiceScope>
    - Reads session via auth() from @/auth
    - Throws "Authentication required." if no session or no user.id
    - Reads workspaceId from session (cached in session callback to avoid extra DB query)
    - Returns { ownerId: userId, workspaceId }
    - This single function replaces every SINGLE_USER_SCOPE reference

  getOptionalAuth(): Promise<ServiceScope | null>
    - Non-throwing variant for conditional UI in server components

  Performance note: workspaceId is cached in the session callback during session read.
  No extra DB query per server action call — auth() already hits the DB for session validation.

