Phase 10.5 — Server action migration (the big swap)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Replace all SINGLE_USER_SCOPE / placeholder usage with await requireAuth().
Six migration patterns:

Pattern A — Direct scope swap (5 files, ~24 functions):
  Files: ledger.ts, files.ts, protocols.ts, drafts.ts, projectCopilot.ts
  Before: return listStudies(SINGLE_USER_SCOPE, projectId);
  After:  const scope = await requireAuth(); return listStudies(scope, projectId);

Pattern B — Remove ensureSingleUserSeed (1 file, 5 functions):
  File: projects.ts
  Remove all ensureSingleUserSeed() calls (provisioning now in Auth.js createUser event).
  Replace SINGLE_USER_SCOPE with await requireAuth().

Pattern C — assertProjectAccess swap (1 file, 2 functions):
  File: extraction.ts
  assertProjectAccess(SINGLE_USER_SCOPE, projectId) → assertProjectAccess(scope, projectId)

Pattern D — Auth gate only (3 files, ~12 functions):
  Files: ai.ts, summarize-conversation.ts, usage.ts
  Add await requireAuth() at top as a gate. Scope not passed deeper yet.
  summarize-conversation.ts: queries conversations by ID with no ownership check — add gate.
  usage.ts: queries AIUsage by projectId only — add gate + scope filtering.

Pattern E — Replace placeholder userId (2 files, ~12 functions):
  File: conversations.ts
    Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER_ID, PLACEHOLDER_WORKSPACE_ID, getCurrentUserContext().
    Replace with: const { ownerId: userId, workspaceId } = await requireAuth();
  File: agent.ts
    Replace hardcoded "single-user" fallbacks with requireAuth().
    Currently uses: userId || "single-user" — must get userId from session instead.

Pattern F — Secure userId params (1 file, ~18 functions):
  File: memory.ts
  User memory functions currently accept userId from client (insecure).
  Change signatures to read userId from session:
    getUserMemoryAction(userId, key)  → getUserMemoryAction(key)
    getUserMemoriesAction(userId, opts) → getUserMemoriesAction(opts)
    searchUserMemoriesAction(userId, q) → searchUserMemoriesAction(q)
    setUserMemoryAction(input) → inject userId from requireAuth() into input
  Update client-side callers accordingly.

  Migration checklist (14 action files):
    projects.ts                5 functions   Pattern B
    ledger.ts                  7 functions   Pattern A
    files.ts                   8 functions   Pattern A
    extraction.ts              2 functions   Pattern C
    protocols.ts               2 functions   Pattern A
    drafts.ts                  2 functions   Pattern A
    projectCopilot.ts          2 functions   Pattern A
    ai.ts                      8 functions   Pattern D
    summarize-conversation.ts  1 function    Pattern D
    usage.ts                   1 function    Pattern D
    notes.ts                   ~4 functions  Pattern D (no auth at all currently)
    agent.ts                   ~4 functions  Pattern E (hardcoded "single-user")
    conversations.ts           8 functions   Pattern E
    memory.ts                 ~18 functions  Pattern F

  Service layer fix (not an action file):
    lib/server/ai/ai-service.ts — has "single-user" hardcoded at ~2 locations
